## Smoke run

One heavy-run wrapper, `HOME=/tmp/opencode/readers-smoke-1`, so that the print folder resolves inside
the temporary home and no file goes into `~/Desktop/print-ready/` (`jr-green-75cc5e54-smoke.txt`).
`--proof --workbook` gives `Storytime-Advantage-L2-Readers-W01-v1_PDFX-1a.pdf`: 6 pages,
594.96 x 841.92 pts, PDF 1.3, PDF/X-1a:2001, "All checks pass", 18 hits of "PICTURE MISSING" (9 for
each reader). `--proof --a3-color` gives two files of 12 pages each at 841.92 x 1191.12 pts, 9 hits
each, and no `GTS_PDFX` output intent (FR-5.8). Observation for the Check task: Chrome writes 0.57 pt
more height than the 1190.55 pt A3 target, as it writes 0.03 pt more for the A4 student book; a later
A3 page-size check needs a small slack.

## Blocked runs of this role (the record)

- The first run found two Red conflicts in the reader contract (a per-book root was assumed for a
  shared A4 leaf, and the A3 pictures were compared by index against the imposed order). Red r3 fixed
  both in `c294f4b6`. The reader code then passed 10 of 10.
- The second run blocked on two picture-list expectations that version 4 contradicts (the week 8
  guard "zero rows" and the 53-key R16 inventory). Red 4b r3 fixed both in `ccdf934c`; the adversarial,
  contract-r3, and contract-v2 files then gave 104 passed on the working tree.
- Neither block changed a committed Red test from this role.

